{
    "display_name": "the Sign of the Fish",
    "_doc": "Play-test 8, ask 8 (call BX): the river folk's lodging house, its common room open; its beds are always full. Laid out by tools/build_interiors.py.",
    "people": [
        {
            "name": "Mother Rook",
            "unit": "town_innkeeper",
            "facing": [
                0,
                1
            ],
            "recruit": false,
            "talk": {
                "hello": [
                    "Ale or pie. There's no third thing.",
                    "River folk sleep here. Land folk drink here and go home. Which are you?"
                ],
                "ask": [
                    {
                        "q": "Why the Sign of the Fish?",
                        "a": "My grandfather caught one the size of a door, the year the river froze. The sign's the fish. The door's the door."
                    },
                    {
                        "q": "Who drinks here?",
                        "a": "Bargemen, pilots, anyone who works the river below the walls. They'd sooner sleep on their boats, but the boats are full of cargo."
                    },
                    {
                        "q": "Have you a room?",
                        "a": "Full. Always full. The barges come in faster than they go out. Try the Flagon."
                    }
                ],
                "news": true,
                "sells": [
                    {
                        "item": "ale_flask",
                        "restock": true
                    },
                    {
                        "item": "bread",
                        "restock": true
                    },
                    {
                        "item": "meat_pie",
                        "restock": true
                    }
                ],
                "shop": "Ale, bread and a pie. Don't ask what's in the pie.",
                "bye": "Mind the step down. It's wet. It's always wet."
            },
            "cell": [
                12,
                2
            ]
        },
        {
            "name": "Jory the Pilot",
            "unit": "town_fisher",
            "facing": [
                1,
                0
            ],
            "recruit": false,
            "talk": {
                "hello": [
                    "You're not river folk. Your boots are too dry.",
                    "Pull up a stool, if you can find one that doesn't wobble."
                ],
                "ask": [
                    {
                        "q": "What does a pilot do?",
                        "a": "Takes a barge through the shallows below the walls without putting it on the gravel. Easy, if you know where the gravel is. I know where the gravel is."
                    },
                    {
                        "q": "Is the river safe?",
                        "a": "Safer than the road, these days. Things from the gates don't care for running water. Mostly."
                    },
                    {
                        "q": "Have you been up the Tower?",
                        "a": "No. I've been down the river to the sea and back twenty times. That's far enough from home for anyone."
                    }
                ],
                "bye": "Mind the gravel."
            },
            "cell": [
                4,
                4
            ]
        },
        {
            "name": "a bargeman asleep",
            "unit": "town_farmer",
            "facing": [
                0,
                1
            ],
            "chatter": [
                "Mm. Not my watch.",
                "Wake me at the lock."
            ],
            "cell": [
                10,
                7
            ]
        }
    ],
